{{also|Send|SEND|Sënd}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sent- (go)}}
From {{inh|en|enm|senden}}, from {{inh|en|ang|sendan|t=to send, cause to go}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*sandijan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*sandijaną}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro||*sont-eye-|t=to cause to go}}, causative of {{m|ine-pro|*sent-|t=to walk, travel}}. The noun is from the verb.

{{rel-top|Cognates}}
Cognate with {{cog|stq|seende|t=to send}}, {{cog|nl|zenden|t=to send}}, {{cog|de|senden|t=to send}}, {{cog|da|-}} and {{cog|no|-}} {{m|da|sende|t=to send}}, {{cog|sv|sända|t=to send}}, {{cog|is|senda|t=to send}}. Related also to {{cog|ang|sand}}, {{m|ang|sond|t=a sending, mission, message}}. See also [[sith]]. {{rel-bottom}}

