===Alternative forms===
* {{l|sq|senë|senë}} {{qualifier|Gheg}} <ref>[https://archive.org/details/fialuurivoghels00junggoog/page/n156/mode/2up Fialuur i voghel Sccyp e ltinisct (Small Dictionary of Albanian and Latin), page 139 : senn], by P. Jak Junkut, 1895, {{w|Shkodër|Sckoder}}</ref>

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sq|sqj-pro|*tsjam tam}}, from {{inh|sq|ine-pro|*kiom tom}}, a sequence of two pronouns in neuter of which the first is related to 'se'.<ref>{{R:sq:Orel:1998|page=394}}</ref> Alternatively from {{inh|sq|sqj-pro|*tśe enta}}, literally 'this being', the first element from {{m|sqj-pro|*kwe-||how, what}}, or {{m|sqj-pro|*k̂(e)||this}}, while the second one being a gerundive or a participle of a disused verb, close to {{cog|la|-ēns}} (participal ending), {{cog|la-med|ens||being}} (hence {{cog|it|ente||entity, body, being}}), and {{cog|grc|ὤν}} (present participle).

